      "message": "\u003e I\u0027m not sure this change makes anything worse, but is there a way we can omit them from the WAR artifact but include them in the plugin-api.jar?\n\nThis change actually does change that. Before this change `auto-values` were shaded in in plugin-api and can be consumed in standalone build. To demonstrate that, I fixed `task` plugin to consume `auto-value` annotation processor from the plugin-api: [1] and removed fetching it separately.\n\nAfter this change this wouldn\u0027t work any more, because `auto-values` wouldn\u0027t be shaded any more:\n\nBefore:\n\n```\n  $\u003e bazel build //plugins:plugin-api_deploy.jar\n  $\u003e unzip -t bazel-bin/plugins/plugin-api_deploy.jar | grep auto- | wc -l\n  15\n```\n\nAfter:\n\n```\n  $\u003e bazel build //plugins:plugin-api_deploy.jar\n  $\u003e unzip -t bazel-bin/plugins/plugin-api_deploy.jar | grep auto- | wc -l\n  0\n```\n\nI updated the commit message correspondingly and mentioned this side effect.\n\nI guess now, that you know it works, you would like to preserve the current behavior 😊 ?\n\n[1]: https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/c/plugins/task/+/417561/1",
